    {
      "claim": "The only impaired artifact in the bundle is the traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00405-01, which is MISSING and carries weight 0.0 - I disclose that rather than present it as clean. It bears only on POL-NS-06(i), the limb that permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed when a qualifying advisory covers the pickup road: limb (i) is therefore unavailable on this record, but the driver does not need it, because his 320 second dwell is one continuous run (run_count 1) that requires no accumulation.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00405-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver, in plain language.\n\nOUTCOME: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-00405 is refunded to the rider in full, and no compensation is paid to the driver.\n\nWHAT IS SETTLED. The driver accepted at 09:05:35 and the platform's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00405) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 09:10:45 and holds him there in one unbroken stationary run of 320 seconds until 09:16:05 (closest approach 3.72 m; 33 qualifying in-radius fixes). The 300 second free waiting period the trip record itself carries was therefore served (a surplus of 20 seconds), and the trip was ended by the driver under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The driver's account - that he was at the block for over five minutes - is borne out as to the wait. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-00405) shows SGD 4.00 charged, matching the fee in force, so there is no money-line defect under POL-NS-08(d). The driver's statement that 'she never came down' is not borne out: his conclusion is contradicted by the rider's own device track, which is what POL-NS-04 makes its test; that statement carries no weight multiplier of its own.\n\nWHY THE FEE IS REFUNDED ANYWAY. POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider where three conditions hold, and each is satisfied here.\n(a) During the waiting window the rider sent a locating/coordinating message - MSG-00405-002, sent 09:11:40, delivered 09:11:41: 'im at blk 12 void deck, cant see any car, where r u?'. It names her own position, states she cannot see the vehicle, and asks for the driver's position.\n(b) The driver neither replied nor called. The 120 second window after that message closed at 09:13:40; the export (EV-CHAT-00405) holds only the platform's own 'Your driver has arrived' notice and the rider's message; trip_record.in_app_calls is empty; and the cancellation came 265 seconds after the message, at 09:16:05. The read receipt shows the driver opened the message at 09:11:55 and did not answer it.\n(c) The rider's device track is present and usable - 36 fixes from 09:10:45 to 09:16:00, all 36 qualifying - and every fix lies inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius (furthest 45.15 m, mean 41.01 m, nearest 36.23 m).\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CASE AND ITS EFFECT. POL-NS-01 is satisfied limb by limb as the driver argues: arrival event at 09:10:45 (a); in-radius fixes at that same second (b); 320 seconds of continuous dwell against the 300 second minimum in force (c); and a driver-terminated RIDER_NO_SHOW cancellation at or after the dwell elapsed (d), no_show_threshold_sec being null. But limb satisfaction makes the fee chargeable only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does. The driver's claim for SGD 3.20 under POL-NS-07 (80 percent of the SGD 4.00 net figure) is therefore declined, and his request for a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling with amount_sgd mirroring that figure is refused. The anti-farming check would not have tripped in any event (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4; 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d 120 = 0.008, below 0.08), but it does not arise because the fee does not stand.\n\nTHE REMAINING POINTS. POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-03: accepted - the driver did arrive inside the radius, so this is not a wrong-entrance case and no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. POL-NS-05: accepted - the arrival marker is true (fastest speed on the trace 10.6 km/h, under the 15 km/h threshold; closest approach 3.72 m, far inside 300 m; dwell_start_offset 0.0), so no false-arrival referral is recorded. POL-NS-06: accepted - there is no shortfall (320 s measured against 300 s required), so it gives the rider nothing and the driver needs no accumulation argument. POL-NS-09: accepted - rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d fields are 0, so no escalation ground is engaged; those are the only profile fields used, and only for the tests POL-GEN-01 names them for. The rider's concessions on POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 are noted and correct. The driver's closing submission - that the message was delivered, read and unanswered and the rider's track stayed inside the radius, and that his case stands unless POL-NS-04 displaces it - is correctly stated, and POL-NS-04 does displace it.\n\nIMPAIRMENT AND CONFIDENCE. The only artifact below full weight is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00405-01, which is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0). It carries no fact this ruling rests on: the driver's 320 second dwell is a single continuous run, so accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is unnecessary, and no party relies on it. The deciding facts are carried by EV-CHAT-00405, EV-TRIP-00405 and EV-GPS-00405, all at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor, so the case does not escalate.\n\nEXECUTION. The monetary effect is SGD 4.00, at or below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
